      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previously, there was a check on `num_vdos`, and an invalid value would not write anything to `vdo`. Now, an invalid value of `vdo_index` will write to `vdo` up to that index. Furthermore, it now appears possible to use this function to read more times from `vdos` than it actually contains elements. Both of these properties seem surprising to me.\n\nIs this what the RTS54xx actually does?",
      "revId": "b9914d391a6d94f86ba6e2502f42b79f068f7f72",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d8f1b5e_7fa2f8f6",
        "filename": "zephyr/emul/emul_realtek_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 801,
